.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt HALITE 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm halite
.Nd configuration management and remote execution for a fleet
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a hub, a node agent and an HTTP API.
The hub holds the state tree, the pillar data and the policy, and is the
certificate authority for the fleet.
A node runs on every managed machine and keeps a mutually authenticated
connection to the hub.
The API exposes the hub to scripts and other systems.
.Pp
There are three programs:
.Bl -tag -width "halite-node" -compact
.It Xr halite-hub 8
the hub.
.It Xr halite-node 8
the node agent, which also applies state locally with
.Fl Fl local .
.It Xr halite-api 8
the HTTP API.
.El
.Sh CONCEPTS
.Bl -tag -width "pillar"
.It state
A declaration of how a machine should be, written in an SLS file.
Applying it makes the machine match; applying it again changes nothing,
and that is what idempotent means here.
.It grain
A fact a node reports about itself, such as its operating system.
.It pillar
Data the hub gives to the nodes selected for it, and to no others.
.It beacon
A watcher on a node that turns a local condition into an event.
.It reactor
A rule on the hub that turns an event into work.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/halite/hub.yaml" -compact
.It Pa /etc/halite
configuration on Linux; on FreeBSD,
.Pa /usr/local/etc/halite .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr halite-sls 5 ,
.Xr halite-policy 5 ,
.Xr halite-hub 8 ,
.Xr halite-node 8 ,
.Xr halite-api 8
.Pp
The Handbook, in the
.Pa handbook/
directory of a release archive, is the complete documentation; begin
with its first chapter.
